==German==
[[Image:MexicanChairs.jpg|thumb|225px|Stühle in Mexiko — Chairs in Mexico.]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|stuol}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stuol}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stōlaz}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|stoel}}, {{cog|en|stool}}, {{cog|sv|stol}}; ultimately from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*steh₂-}} and thus related to {{m|de|stehen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃtuːl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Stuhl.OGG|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Stuhls|gen2=Stuhles|Stühle|Stühlchen}}

# a [[chair]] (to sit on)
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe die ganze Zeit auf meinem '''Stuhl''' gesessen!|I've been sitting on my chair the whole time!}}
# a [[chair]] (professorship)
#: {{ux|de|Professor Martin wurde überraschend auf den '''Stuhl''' berufen.|Surprisingly, Professor Martin received the professorship.}}
# {{lb|de|euphemism|mainly used in medical professions}} [[feces]], [[stool]]
#: ''Herr Urkwicz hatte heute wieder sehr weichen '''Stuhl'''.'' — Today Mr Urkwicz again had very soft feces.
# {{lb|de|medicine|formal}} [[stool]]

